---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import { SITE_TITLE } from '../consts';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title={`Privacy | ${SITE_TITLE}`}
			description="What Autophagy collects, where it lives, and what we share with anyone else. Short answer: nothing leaves your device."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<h1>Privacy</h1>
			<p><em>Effective 15 May 2026.</em></p>

			<h2>Summary</h2>
			<p>
				The Autophagy iOS app collects no personal data. Every session you log
				(fasting, exercise, cold, sauna, breathing) is stored on your device only.
				Nothing is uploaded to our servers because we have no servers that hold
				user data. We don't use third-party analytics inside the app, no tracking
				SDKs, no advertising networks.
			</p>
			<p>
				The marketing website at autophagy.fit uses Google Analytics for basic
				traffic measurement (which pages people read, how they got here). That's
				it.
			</p>

			<h2>The iOS app</h2>

			<h3>What we store</h3>
			<p>The app stores the following on your device only, via Apple's SwiftData framework:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Your logged sessions: fasting periods, exercise, cold immersion, sauna, Reset Breathing rounds, and any notes you attach</li>
				<li>Your preferences: daily target, reminder time, appearance choice, founder-pricing reservation status</li>
			</ul>
			<p>
				None of this leaves the device. There is no Autophagy account, no sign-in,
				no sync to a remote server. If you delete the app, the data is gone.
			</p>

			<h3>What we don't collect</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>No email address, name, phone number, or any other identifying information</li>
				<li>No location data</li>
				<li>No advertising identifiers</li>
				<li>No HealthKit data in v1. HealthKit integration is planned for v2 and will be opt-in with the standard iOS permission prompt</li>
				<li>No analytics events or usage telemetry from inside the app</li>
				<li>No data sold or shared with third parties</li>
			</ul>

			<h3>Notifications</h3>
			<p>
				If you turn on the daily reminder in Settings, the app schedules a local
				iOS notification at your chosen time. The notification is generated and
				delivered entirely on your device. We don't operate a push-notification
				server.
			</p>

			<h3>Content tab</h3>
			<p>
				The in-app content library loads articles from autophagy.fit using
				Apple's WKWebView. When you open an article, your device makes a standard
				HTTP request to autophagy.fit, the same as visiting the site in a
				browser. That request is logged by Cloudflare (who host the site) in
				standard server access logs. We don't link those logs back to individuals.
			</p>

			<h2>The website (autophagy.fit)</h2>

			<h3>Google Analytics</h3>
			<p>
				We use Google Analytics 4 to understand which pages get read, where
				visitors come from, and roughly how the site is performing. Google
				Analytics sets a cookie in your browser and reports aggregated traffic
				data back to us. We don't view or store individual visitor identities.
			</p>
			<p>
				If you'd rather not be counted, install any standard ad/tracker blocker,
				or set your browser to send the Do Not Track signal. Google Analytics
				doesn't enforce that signal but most blockers do.
			</p>

			<h3>Cloudflare</h3>
			<p>
				The site is hosted on Cloudflare Pages. Cloudflare keeps standard server
				access logs (IP address, request URL, user agent, timestamp) for the
				purposes of operating their service and protecting against abuse. We
				don't read these logs.
			</p>

			<h3>What we don't do on the website</h3>
			<ul>
				<li>No advertising or ad networks</li>
				<li>No data sold to third parties</li>
				<li>No personalised tracking beyond standard analytics</li>
				<li>No cookies set by Autophagy itself, only by Google Analytics</li>
			</ul>

			<h2>Your rights</h2>
			<p>
				Because we collect no personal data in the app, there's nothing for us to
				disclose, correct, or delete on request. If you want to remove all your
				app data, delete the app from your phone.
			</p>
			<p>
				For website traffic data collected through Google Analytics, you can opt
				out using
				<a href="https://tools.google.com/dlpage/gaoptout">Google's official
				opt-out browser extension</a>.
			</p>

			<h2>Children</h2>
			<p>
				Autophagy is not directed at children under 13. If you believe a child
				has provided us with information through any of our services (we can't
				see what that would be, since we don't collect anything), please email us
				and we'll review it.
			</p>

			<h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
			<p>
				If we change what data the app or website handles, this page will be
				updated and the effective date at the top revised. Material changes will
				also be announced inside the app on next launch.
			</p>

			<h2>Contact</h2>
			<p>
				Questions about privacy: autophagy@alamex.com
			</p>
			<p>
				Autophagy is operated by Alamex Ltd, a company registered in England and
				Wales.
			</p>
		</main>
		<Footer />
	</body>
</html>
